abstract: >
  General Structure Unfolding Intelligence (GSUI) develops a structural
  framework for studying intelligent processes as controlled unfolding
  from persistent structure. Its canonical form is expressed as
  <Core Structure> +/- <Delta Modification>, with extensions involving
  context, triggering, unfolding space, control policy, evaluation,
  invariant preservation, certification, feedback, structural growth,
  and Structural Self. The repository examines folding and unfolding as
  complementary phases of an intelligence cycle, distinguishes search
  within an existing possibility space from structural unfolding that can
  change future possibility itself, and introduces Structural Self as the
  persistent reference frame relative to which Delta, capability,
  continuity, world-model meaning, and future unfolding are defined.
  GSUI further explores machine-native perception and cognition while
  preserving the principle of human-governable consequential action.

